# Without this file, git falls back to its own per-commit text/binary
# heuristic for every file, including PDFs and PNGs this project commits
# under reports/ and docs/reports/. That heuristic can misclassify a binary
# file as text (a PDF's structure is mostly ASCII operators around binary
# compressed streams), and core.autocrlf then normalizes line endings
# inside it — silently corrupting the binary content in a way lenient
# tooling (qpdf --check, pdftoppm) can tolerate but GitHub's own blob
# viewer does not. Declaring these explicitly removes the heuristic
# entirely for these extensions, checkout and commit alike.
*.pdf binary
*.png binary
